ER AND HE IS NOT HER BABY’S FATHER.” His facial expressions are angry or defensive. There is no physical contact or positive body language.\n- **Frames 12, 13–23:** Tara (in teal) is shown on stage, then running off the set in distress after learning “SHAWN IS NOT HER BABY’S FATHER.” Her body language (running, head down, leaving the set) indicates emotional pain and rejection.\n- **No direct interaction is shown between Shawn and Tara in the same frame.** Their “interaction” is mediated through the host and the DNA test reveal.\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Check setting and relationship type.**\n\n- The setting is clearly the **Maury Povich Show**, a TV studio — a professional, public, and confrontational environment.\n- The context is a **paternity dispute** — inherently personal, emotional, and conflict-driven.\n- Their relationship is **not professional** — they are not colleagues or business partners. The conflict centers on infidelity, betrayal, and parentage — deeply personal issues.\n- The on-screen text and emotional reactions confirm a **romantic/parental relationship gone sour**, not a professional one.\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Evaluate the answer “3 — They have a professional relationship.”**\n\n❌ This is **incorrect**.\n\n- There is **no evidence** of a professional relationship.\n- All visual and textual cues point to a **personal, romantic, and broken relationship**.\n- The emotional intensity, accusations, and DNA test context are inconsistent with a professional dynamic.\n\n---\n\n✅ **Final Answer: No, the answer ‘3’ is not correct. Shawn and Tara do not have a professional relationship — they have a personal, emotionally charged, and conflicted relationship centered on paternity and betrayal.**'}], 'formatted_responses': ["\n=== Batch 0-30 (30 frames) ===\nFrames: /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/vHlSoxg8WHo/frames/frame_2135.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/vHlSoxg8WHo/frames/frame_2136.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/vHlSoxg8WHo/fr